  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nXSLT is referenced in the GitHub HTML Standard.  GitHub has been informed that Chromium Project proposes, and now has begun to execute, a plan to deprecate XSLT from its browser. An action that will eventually cascade to other browsers, because Chromium is \"open source\".  \n\nHas anyone assessed or polled the GitHub community about the user / subscriber impact? \n\nUse of XSLT in GitHub pages is the reason that I pay for GitHub services.  Client side XSLT is a great solution for using GitHub for more than a code repository . It is simple and powerful, stable, cross-platform, browser agnostic and standards based. No server side code or applications, only static html pages, Style sheets, and XML data.\n\nGitHub has little value to me, my work and the community my project served and supports, without the ability to support client-side processing in a cross-platform, browser agnostic and standards based manner.\n\nIt seems to me that GitHub would want to be an advocate for it's customer and user base, i.e., that any proposal for affecting user access to GitHub repositories and services, such as XSLT, would include options for continuity and reasonable plans for migration that work for for GitHub subscribers and users. \n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n",
